-- title:
--   Module-finiteness of the Drinfeld level-q deformation map
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation ring $W_0$ (a domain) whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ with `F₀.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with respect to the ideal $\bot$ the series `F₀.nthSeries q` is a unit of $k[[X]]$ times `F₀.drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`. Let $R$ be a noetherian local $W_0$-algebra, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with a surjective $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ of kernel $\mathfrak m_R$ satisfying $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \mathrm{alg}_{W_0} = \mathrm{res}_0$, and let $F$ be a commutative formal group law over $R$ reducing to $F_0$, in the sense that $F_0$'s defining bivariate series is the image of $F$'s under $\mathrm{res}_R$. Assume $x_0, x_1 \in \mathfrak m_R$ satisfy `F.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic (maximalIdeal R) q x₀ x₁`, that is `F.nthSeries q` is a unit of $R[[X]]$ times `F.drinfeldDivisor q x₀ x₁` formed with respect to $\mathfrak m_R$, and that $\mathfrak m_R = (x_0, x_1)$. Let $F^{\mathrm u}$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[X]]$ whose reduction along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $F_0$, let $\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to R$ be a $W_0$-algebra map with $\varphi(X) \in \mathfrak m_R$, and let $F'$ be a commutative formal group law over $R$ obtained from $F^{\mathrm u}$ by applying $\varphi$ coefficientwise. Finally let $\psi$ be an isomorphism of formal group laws from $F'$ to $F$, given by a power series over $R$ with zero constant term, unit coefficient in degree one, satisfying the compatibility $\psi \circ F' = F \circ (\psi, \psi)$, and assume every coefficient of $\psi$ reduces modulo $\mathfrak m_R$ to that of $X$, i.e. to $1$ in degree $1$ and $0$ otherwise. Then $\varphi$ is finite: $R$ is a finitely generated $W_0[[X]]$-module via $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the finiteness half of Drinfeld's theorem on deformation rings carrying a level-$q$ Drinfeld basis: the deformation ring is module-finite over the Lubin–Tate power series ring $W_0[[X]]$. It feeds into the statement that such a ring is regular local of Krull dimension two.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FormalGroup_IsDrinfeldBasisAdic_finite_of_lawIso_isBaseChange_powerSeries_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_isComm.lean

